# Exceptions

## Unsupported

The `Unsupported` exception is thrown when an operation or feature is not supported.

### Example

```javascript
try {
    // Code that may throw an exception
} catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof Unsupported) {
        console.error('Unsupported operation:', error.message);
    }
}
